// The Archive's warden (GDR-0130, lead default 20 Oct 2026): the boss at the galaxy's centre, a huge precursor
// construct run by a surviving mind, one of the forty that signed the gate order. Four sections, each on sentinel cores
// of its own, joined by one bridge block each: the fore section (two torpedo launchers, three long cannons, a fission
// reactor), the heart (two beam lasers at its front corners, two prism wards, point defence, a fusion reactor, two
// cores, and at its back the torch drive, two thrusters, two fission reactors and a gyro), and a wing on each side (a
// wide shield emitter, point defence, an ion cannon in front, a rocket pod and a long cannon facing back). Radiators everywhere,
// plated in precursor alloy. It flies `archive_warden`, whose rules switch with its hull share: every section shot off
// counts as lost (the fore about 14 %, a wing 11 %), so the heart holds off at range while it is whole, closes in once a
// section is gone and charges when it is down to about half. A section shot off fights on alone with the same rules,
// turning where it drifts. Not tagged `enemy`: the test range's waves keep to the rim's. PLACEHOLDER layout
// (docs/results/core-band-2026-10-20.md).
